{"id": "kezar-architect-state-contracting-ban", "title": "Kezar Pavilion replaced its historic architect under a City contracting ban", "seconds": 57.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "43e3a2bc42add42e", "words": 142, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "A specialist was assessing historic features at Kezar Pavilion.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.86, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Why", "replace", "the", "specialist?"], "sub": "Kezar Pavilion"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.74, 0.91, 1.46, 1.98, 2.48, 2.61, 3.0]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "The architect’s firm was acquired by a company in a state on the City’s prohibited list.", "t0": 3.98, "t1": 8.82, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bond", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller", "text": "A change in ownership", "mark": "A change in ownership"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.78, 1.13, 1.32, 1.83, 1.99, 2.09, 2.55, 2.64, 2.73, 3.1, 3.21, 3.33, 3.71, 4.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "The City hired a replacement. The Controller reported that this added time.", "t0": 8.94, "t1": 13.79, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Replacement specialist"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.49, 0.83, 0.92, 2.26, 2.46, 3.04, 3.52, 3.7, 3.98, 4.35]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The contracting restrictions began in 2016 in response to state limits on LGBT rights.", "t0": 13.91, "t1": 20.22, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "ordinance", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors", "text": "2016 contracting ordinance", "mark": "2016 contracting ordinance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.83, 1.49, 1.88, 2.0, 2.36, 3.09, 3.28, 3.79, 3.95, 4.33, 4.78, 5.03, 5.74]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "In one year 35 departments approved 538 waivers across City purchasing.", "t0": 20.34, "t1": 26.12, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "waivers", "kicker": "San Francisco Budget and Legislative Analyst", "text": "July 2021 to July 2022", "mark": "July 2021 to July 2022"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.8, 1.42, 2.01, 2.49, 2.85, 3.24, 3.81, 4.33, 4.74, 5.04]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "In 48 cases the only responsive bidders came from covered states.", "t0": 26.24, "t1": 31.18, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "48", "label": "Waivers with only responsive bidders from covered states"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.82, 1.54, 1.8, 2.14, 2.81, 3.27, 3.58, 3.84, 4.28]}, {"scene": "scope", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The disaster-response component was two years behind its earlier schedule.", "t0": 31.4, "t1": 35.52, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bond", "kicker": "San Francisco Controller", "text": "Disaster-response component", "mark": "Disaster-response component"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 1.19, 1.71, 1.88, 2.15, 2.48, 2.87, 3.08, 3.53]}, {"scene": "scope", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "Pandemic response and more complex site assessments also took time.", "t0": 35.64, "t1": 39.89, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Other reasons for delay"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 1.2, 1.39, 1.63, 2.21, 2.47, 3.14, 3.56, 3.81]}, {"scene": "scope", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The preliminary review helped avoid a lengthy environmental impact report.", "t0": 40.01, "t1": 44.19, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Historic review"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.77, 1.23, 1.51, 1.87, 1.95, 2.37, 3.13, 3.66]}, {"scene": "scope", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "In 2026 the project team projected a public opening in 2031.", "t0": 44.31, "t1": 48.82, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "relationship", "context": "Project schedule", "heading": "Two published forecasts", "source": "faq", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "June 2023 bond report", "value": "Completion in 2027"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "January 2026 FAQ", "value": "Public opening in 2031"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 1.13, 1.25, 1.7, 1.93, 2.4, 2.48, 2.9, 3.31, 3.41, 3.77]}, {"scene": "scope", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The Controller did not quantify the cost or time attributable to replacing the specialist.", "t0": 48.94, "t1": 53.92, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Time attributable to replacement", "Additional cost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.67, 0.85, 1.05, 1.62, 1.73, 2.2, 2.39, 2.68, 3.35, 3.49, 4.06, 4.15]}, {"scene": "scope", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 54.04, "t1": 56.65, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.8, 0.97, 1.29, 1.39, 1.48, 1.78, 2.11]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Replacing the architect", "scope": "The project schedule"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "person"}